{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1430698-v20-vicissitude-and-physical-impediments","id":1430698,"title":"V20 Vicissitude and physical impediments","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-01-01T17:06:02-08:00","id":1430698,"title":"V20 Vicissitude and physical impediments","content":"I am curious to the limits of Vicissitude, and I wonder if applied to a mortal, it can: <ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Heal physical impediments like nearsightedness (myopia)?</li> <li>Heal physical impediments like missing organs?</li> <li>Identify cancerous cells?</li> <li>Remove cancerous cells?</li> <li>Alter cancerous cells so they are no longer cancerous?</li> <li>Remove body fat from the body (liposuction)?</li> </ol><br /> Thanks for the time and attention.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4967,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","user":"lbeaumanior","date":". 01-02-2021, 11:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-01T21:51:45-08:00","id":1430725,"title":"","content":"The fundamental point and the reason why its so cool (pre-V5 Vicissitude of course) was that it is a completely freeform Discipline that allows you to do anything within the realm of your thought/imagination. Everything you listed can be done (though I'd have it that you'd atleast have a few dots in medicine to even know what your doing; which is the reason most Tzimisce embrace medical professionals). Just go crazy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-02T04:02:05-08:00","id":1430736,"title":"","content":"If you can do something with mundane surgery, you can do it with Vicissitude, probably a little better. Of course, knowing how to do something with mundane surgery requires a lot of knowledge. I don't believe vicissitude alone has any 'identify' ability, but it's not a coincidence that Tzmisce have Auspex too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-02T04:51:44-08:00","id":1430738,"title":"","content":"1, definitely, 2, Maybe, probably with rituals, like those used to make the melded war ghouls, 3,4,5 probably not, cellular manipulation is stretching it, but doing what a surgeon could, certainly. 6. Yes, this is used as an example in fact (Death and the Soul Tzim can tell you exactly how much you can remove before the patient dies, they have experiments to prove it). Vis would be the tool used, you would need the knowledge of what exactly to do, Auspex would help for assessing things as well","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-02T08:45:29-08:00","id":1430751,"title":"","content":"<ol class=\"decimal\"><li><b>Heal physical impediments like nearsightedness (myopia)? </b>Yes, with enough medicine</li> <li><b>Heal physical impediments like missing organs?</b> Yes, with enough medicine and a source of flesh or spare organs</li> <li><b>Identify cancerous cells? </b>No. The discipline doesn't grant knowledge.</li> <li><b>Remove cancerous cells? </b>Yes.</li> <li><b>Alter cancerous cells so they are no longer cancerous?</b> In theory it allows cellular alteration, but this is pushing genetic alteration, which is beyond what it can do. A clever use might be able to figure out how to do this.</li> <li><b>Remove body fat from the body (liposuction)?</b> Yes. This one is trivial for them to do.</li> </ol><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1VN49Y7tH2ZV0l7Hx65RWX1ez-Q9Lst-8ZTyTJeCTpxM/\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerer 20th</a> homebrew and my update to <a href=\"http://immortalthegathering.blogspot.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Highlander: the Gathering</a> for 20th Anniversary edition.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2414-theoutlander523","name":"theoutlander523","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2414_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-02T11:46:29-08:00","id":1430768,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1430698-v20-vicissitude-and-physical-impediments#post1430698\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am curious to the limits of Vicissitude, and I wonder if it applied to a mortal, it can:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Heal physical impediments like nearsightedness (myopia)?</li> <li>Heal physical impediments like missing organs?</li> <li>Identify cancerous cells?</li> <li>Remove cancerous cells?</li> <li>Alter cancerous cells so they are no longer cancerous?</li> <li>Remove body fat from the body (liposuction)?</li> </ol><br /> Thanks for the time and attention.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would say anything that requires extreme precision on a micro level is out of the question. In most editions the use of viscissitude is likened to working stiff clay. Adjusting the focusing properties of the eye is far too delicate for working clay. Bear in mind that you are doing this with your hands and not with surgical tools. Further more anything too small to be grasped or manipulated by the hands/claws/tentacles of the viscissitude user is also likely to be out of the question, which means manipulating individual cells or adjusting things on that level isn't viable.<br /> <br /> There is a reason why Vozhd construction often requires Kuldonic sorcery to bridge the gap between what Vicissitude can and can't do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-02T14:47:57-08:00","id":1430794,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1430698-v20-vicissitude-and-physical-impediments?p=1430768#post1430768\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Adjusting the focusing properties of the eye is far too delicate for working clay. Bear in mind that you are doing this with your hands and not with surgical tools. Further more anything too small to be grasped or manipulated by the hands/claws/tentacles of the viscissitude user is also likely to be out of the question, which means manipulating individual cells or adjusting things on that level isn't viable.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yet Viscissitude allows the Tzimisce to mimic another person, including eye color. How would one mold oneself into earth or mist? Clay is just a metaphor. Dominate applied to flesh is what does the work, not clumsy fingers, hence the Amalgam.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26600-nehekhare","name":"Nehekhare","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-02T14:57:14-08:00","id":1430795,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nehekhare</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1430698-v20-vicissitude-and-physical-impediments?p=1430794#post1430794\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yet Viscissitude allows the Tzimisce to mimic another person, including eye color. How would one mold oneself into earth or mist? Clay is just a metaphor. Dominate applied to flesh is what does the work, not clumsy fingers, hence the Amalgam.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for the answer, but I am asking for V20, no amalgams there, it is a discipline of its own.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-02T16:17:35-08:00","id":1430806,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nehekhare</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1430698-v20-vicissitude-and-physical-impediments?p=1430794#post1430794\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yet Viscissitude allows the Tzimisce to mimic another person, including eye color. How would one mold oneself into earth or mist? Clay is just a metaphor. Dominate applied to flesh is what does the work, not clumsy fingers, hence the Amalgam.</div> </div> </div> </div>In V20 and earlier versions, Viscissitude requires direct manual manipulation when using the power on others. So the subject of how Protean earth meld or Mist form is applied doesn't apply.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-02T19:39:40-08:00","id":1430821,"title":"","content":"I think the level 5 power demonstrates the potential of Vicissitude to alter tissues on a cellular level, but one would have to develop a custom elder discipline power to work such comprehensive changes on others.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-02T20:29:44-08:00","id":1430822,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1430698-v20-vicissitude-and-physical-impediments#post1430698\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am curious to the limits of Vicissitude, and I wonder if applied to a mortal, it can: <ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Heal physical impediments like nearsightedness (myopia)?</li> <li>Heal physical impediments like missing organs?</li> <li>Identify cancerous cells?</li> <li>Remove cancerous cells?</li> <li>Alter cancerous cells so they are no longer cancerous?</li> <li>Remove body fat from the body (liposuction)?</li> </ol><br /> <br /> Thanks for the time and attention.</div> </div> </div> </div>The definitive answer is... maybe.<br /> <br /> At different times Vicissitude has been interpreted as to be so so evil that is cannot even be used to heal wounds and probably causes cancer when used on the living. Vicissitude is a power provided Tzimisce and Kupula, a vampire god-thing and demon-lord respectively, so there is something to this argument.<br /> <br /> Even aside from that, what you describe here would have different levels of difficultly. Removing fat would be comparatively simple, say a couple of success at a difficulty of 5. Fixing myopia would require a great deal of finesse and attention to detail, and require multiple successes at a higher difficult, say three or four success at a 7 not succeed and not blind the target. A lot of Tzimisce - usually the only ones to possess Vicissitude - find it easier to smash things that to repair or build things.<br /> <br /> I doubt it could be used to find cancer, but it probably could be used to remove a tumor.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-02T21:17:25-08:00","id":1430826,"title":"","content":"What do you guys think of the Dark Ages version of Vicissitude that swaps out the level 5 power?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24221-vamps-like-us","name":"Vamps Like Us","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-03T01:04:49-08:00","id":1430842,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vamps Like Us</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1430698-v20-vicissitude-and-physical-impediments?p=1430826#post1430826\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What do you guys think of the Dark Ages version of Vicissitude that swaps out the level 5 power?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The sever body parts and have them slither around thing? It's...interesting I guess?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-03T01:33:05-08:00","id":1430845,"title":"","content":"I prefer bloodform but honestly it should kinda be both?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-03T01:49:39-08:00","id":1430850,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1430698-v20-vicissitude-and-physical-impediments?p=1430845#post1430845\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I prefer bloodform but honestly it should kinda be both?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Having both in one pick may be a bit to good, I would go for bloodform over Thing mode (Addams family, not horror movie mode <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-03T08:43:19-08:00","id":1430871,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1430698-v20-vicissitude-and-physical-impediments#post1430698\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am curious to the limits of Vicissitude, and I wonder if applied to a mortal, it can:<br /> <ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Heal physical impediments like nearsightedness (myopia)?</li> <li>Heal physical impediments like missing organs?</li> <li>Identify cancerous cells?</li> <li>Remove cancerous cells?</li> <li>Alter cancerous cells so they are no longer cancerous?</li> <li>Remove body fat from the body (liposuction)?</li> </ol><br /> <br /> Thanks for the time and attention.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for the answers.I had thought that: <ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Would be iffy, REALLY high Dexterity + Auspex + Vicissitude + high dots in Medicine would do; but perhaps still impossible.</li> <li>Possible, but difficult, like a very limited <i>Vozhd </i>creation, and you need &quot;donated&quot; organs and/or a lot of body mass to work with.</li> <li>Impossible (it seems more something that Vicissitude + Auspex + high dots in Medicine would do)</li> <li>Once 3 is done, doing 4 seemed just tissue removal (as long as the removal was not life-threatening, like removing the whole esophagus).</li> <li>Seemed flat out impossible.</li> <li>I was confused on whether the mass had to stay in the body, thinking of the level 2 power, but yes, removal seems very simple.</li> </ol><br /> <br /> A final question, instead of doing 1, would it be possible to transplant somebody else eyes and make them work?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-03T09:51:33-08:00","id":1430881,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1430698-v20-vicissitude-and-physical-impediments?p=1430871#post1430871\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thanks for the answers.I had thought that:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Would be iffy, REALLY high Dexterity + Auspex + Vicissitude + high dots in Medicine would do; but perhaps still impossible.</li> <li>Possible, but difficult, like a very limited <i>Vozhd </i>creation, and you need &quot;donated&quot; organs and/or a lot of body mass to work with.</li> <li>Impossible (it seems more something that Vicissitude + Auspex + high dots in Medicine would do)</li> <li>Once 3 is done, doing 4 seemed just tissue removal (as long as the removal was not life-threatening, like removing the whole esophagus).</li> <li>Seemed flat out impossible.</li> <li>I was confused on whether the mass had to stay in the body, thinking of the level 2 power, but yes, removal seems very simple.</li> </ol><br /> <br /> A final question, instead of doing 1, would it be possible to transplant somebody else eyes and make them work?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Merging seems to take Koldunic Sorcery, as Vozhd creation is iirc a ritual (At least it was in Dark Ages, the last time I had a character who would want to try it), so functional organ transplants are part sorcery...probably<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-12T08:45:47-07:00","id":1520453,"title":"","content":"This is a bit of necromancy on the thread, but I did not want to create a new one for related questions.<br /> <br /> <br /> Can Vicissitude be used to remove Physical Flaws? <b>Monstrous </b>sets your Appearance to 0, <b>Disfigured </b>tops you at Appearance 2, and <b>Short </b>makes you, well short, but <b>Malleable Visage</b> can change both.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4967,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","user":"lbeaumanior","date":".  Details added. 08-12-2023, 05:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-12T13:07:42-07:00","id":1520470,"title":"","content":"As usual, the straightforward answer would probably be Maybe. I don't know if there was ever an explicit rule on that in any editions.<br /> <br /> My personal answer would probably be Mostly Yes, But It Depends. I've never actually tested the idea, but I've thought about using various Physical Merits or Flaws as an option to expand the possibilities of Vicissitude, particularly the 3rd dot. I'd imagine that it would be an extended action in a lab kind of thing, and you may even need to spend XP to keep it balanced, but I've always liked the idea.<br /> <br /> And yeah, whether or not you could give/take Merits/Flaws that way would probably depend on the technical skill you would imagine that a given feat might require. <br /> <br /> The point about Malleable Visage is a good one, especially regarding the Short Flaw. But regarding the Monstrous Flaw, I'd point out that it goes an extra step and makes gaining Appearance impossible. In contrast, someone reduced to Appearance 0 without also being Monstrous could hypothetically regain Appearance 1 I believe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-12T13:42:00-07:00","id":1520472,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kharnov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1430698-v20-vicissitude-and-physical-impediments?p=1520470#post1520470\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As usual, the straightforward answer would probably be Maybe. I don't know if there was ever an explicit rule on that in any editions.<br /> <br /> My personal answer would probably be Mostly Yes, But It Depends. I've never actually tested the idea, but I've thought about using various Physical Merits or Flaws as an option to expand the possibilities of Vicissitude, particularly the 3rd dot. I'd imagine that it would be an extended action in a lab kind of thing, and you may even need to spend XP to keep it balanced, but I've always liked the idea.<br /> <br /> And yeah, whether or not you could give/take Merits/Flaws that way would probably depend on the technical skill you would imagine that a given feat might require.<br /> <br /> The point about Malleable Visage is a good one, especially regarding the Short Flaw.<b> But regarding the Monstrous Flaw, I'd point out that it goes an extra step and makes gaining Appearance impossible. In contrast, someone reduced to Appearance 0 without also being Monstrous could hypothetically regain Appearance 1 I believe.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for the answer.<br /> <br /> You can lose/gain Merits/Flaws in game, and Vicissitude seems to me one of those methods. The V20 discipline description makes a point of saying you can not remove the Nosferatu or Gangrel curse:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vicissitude V20, p. 241</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Note: Nosferatu always \u201cheal\u201d Vicissitude altera-<br /> tions, at least the ones that make them better-looking.<br /> The ancient curse of the Clan may not be circumvent-<br /> ed through Vicissitude. The same applies to physical<br /> deformities from the Gangrel Clan weakness.\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> And the <b>Disfigured </b>and <b>Monstrous </b>flaws state:<br /> <br /> <i><b>Disfigured (2pt. Flaw)</b><br /> <b>A hideous disfigurement makes your appearance dis-<br /> turbing and memorable.</b> The difficulties of all die rolls<br /> relating to social interaction are increased by two. <b>You<br /> may not have an Appearance rating greater than 2.\u200b</b><br /> <br /> <b>Monstrous (3pt. Flaw)</b><br /> <b>Your physical form was twisted during the Embrace,<br /> and now reflects the Beast that rages inside you. Char-<br /> acters with this Flaw appear to be savage monsters and<br /> have Appearance ratings of zero.</b> Nosferatu and other<br /> bloodlines whose weaknesses cause them to start off<br /> with Appearance zero cannot take this Flaw.\u200b</i><br /> <br /> <br /> There seems to be nothing saying that it can not be cured/fixed. Essentially, with both flaws are you are quite, disturbingly ugly, and Vicissitude 1 mentions a difficulty for increasing Appearance beyond the natural total (0 in the case of those with <b>Monstrous</b>), what in the Flaw description would make it impossible to fix?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-12T14:02:15-07:00","id":1520473,"title":"","content":"Just making it clear that there is something called metastasis, which is when cancer cells are transported throughout the body by blood vessels, when this case comes the cancer spreads and it is not possible to cure and I imagine that vicissitude cannot deal with it so this is something to consider, as for making cancer cells normal, it depends, does vicissitude affect DNA? If this is not the case, even if you can make them return to normal over time, they will revert to the cancerous state.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1430698-v20-vicissitude-and-physical-impediments?p=1430871#post1430871\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A final question, instead of doing 1, would it be possible to transplant somebody else eyes and make them work?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>That depends, if the eye problem is in the cornea it can be cured with a transplant, but if it is in the nerve or brain, no, I don't even know if it's possible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-12T21:18:38-07:00","id":1520498,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1430698-v20-vicissitude-and-physical-impediments?p=1520472#post1520472\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thanks for the answer.<br /> <br /> You can lose/gain Merits/Flaws in game, and Vicissitude seems to me one of those methods. The V20 discipline description makes a point of saying you can not remove the Nosferatu or Gangrel curse:</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with this in principle, which is a big part of why I like it as an approach to expanding Vicissitude use. My only concern is that being able to use Vicissitude in that way without any cost other than downtime might have the potential to get really out of hand, so keeping some kind of tangible cost seems appropriate. But again, I don't have a lot of experience to work with, so I can mostly consider the problem theoretically.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1430698-v20-vicissitude-and-physical-impediments?p=1520472#post1520472\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And the <b>Disfigured </b>and <b>Monstrous </b>flaws state:<br /> <br /> <i><b>Disfigured (2pt. Flaw)</b><br /> <b>A hideous disfigurement makes your appearance dis-<br /> turbing and memorable.</b> The difficulties of all die rolls<br /> relating to social interaction are increased by two. <b>You<br /> may not have an Appearance rating greater than 2.\u200b</b><br /> <br /> <b>Monstrous (3pt. Flaw)</b><br /> <b>Your physical form was twisted during the Embrace,<br /> and now reflects the Beast that rages inside you. Char-<br /> acters with this Flaw appear to be savage monsters and<br /> have Appearance ratings of zero.</b> Nosferatu and other<br /> bloodlines whose weaknesses cause them to start off<br /> with Appearance zero cannot take this Flaw.\u200b</i><br /> <br /> <br /> There seems to be nothing saying that it can not be cured/fixed. Essentially, with both flaws are you are quite, disturbingly ugly, and Vicissitude 1 mentions a difficulty for increasing Appearance beyond the natural total (0 in the case of those with <b>Monstrous</b>), what in the Flaw description would make it impossible to fix?</div> </div> </div> </div>You are correct, my memory failed me there. I was probably a) mixing in the part from Disfigured that puts a cap on max Appearance, or b) mixing in the part from the Nosferatu Curse, treating the Curse and the Flaw as essentially identical when they're only similar.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-12T23:47:00-07:00","id":1520503,"title":"","content":"If we treat Vicissitude as similar to mundane surgery, we must modify the question: can a surgeon cure a person's disfigurement?<br /> <br /> The answer, of course, being &quot;Yes&quot; in many cases. That's what plastic surgery is for.<br /> <br /> So it seems pretty clear that Vicissitude should be able to.<br /> <br /> Mechanically, were I the Storyteller in this scenario, I would mandate that getting rid of the Flaw would require buying it off with XP. It's no fair to the other players if one elects to start the PC with Disfigured or Monstrous, then go get in-universe plastic surgery to immediately correct it, maybe with a temporary dip in Resources to cover the cost. If you want to not be ugly anymore, you have to pay off the chargen points you got.<br /> <br /> The surgery - or in this case the Vicissitude - can merely be thought of as the justification for buying off the Flaw. In much the way the PC might get surgery and physical therapy to buy off the Lame Flaw, or go to rehab to shake off an Addiction.<br /> <br /> Obviously, the above mostly applies to mortals. Vampire PCs are more limited in what methods can change their form on a permanent basis. (And, as an aside, Rehab isn't really a possibility for vampires either, for multiple reasons). Vicissitude's utility is not merely that it's flesh-sculpting magic that goes beyond what mundane surgery can do, and more easily/quickly/safely, it's also necessary to permanently change the undead form. Generation permitting, it would just be a matter of choosing not to spend BP healing the &quot;aggravated wounds&quot; that a change represents. (And if you're paying XP alongside it, I as ST would just make it permanent. You wanted it, you got it).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-13T01:54:36-07:00","id":1520506,"title":"","content":"I always go with the idea of Vicissitude requires literal sculpting of the changes. You could increase height, but that mass needs to come from <i>somewhere</i>, so will probably end up thinner/frailer than what they were before. To increase bone length, well, that bone\u2019s gotta come from somewhere else in you, unless you stretch out what\u2019s already there, and weaken it in the process. <br /> Remove cancer <i>cells</i>, that\u2019s a no, but they could certainly remove a tumour. <br /> <br /> Basically, it lets you use your fingers as scalpels/forceps/clay-shaping tools. I\u2019m not really even a fan of it being able to change eye/hair colour, and only accept it because it\u2019s specifically called out as being possible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27967-caerolion","name":"Caerolion","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-13T02:39:37-07:00","id":1520507,"title":"","content":"I'd say that in my opinion the basics of Vicissitude is that its magical. Hence its mystical nature trumps science and such, mostly.<br /> <br /> I would probably allow a great deal of things to be done if the character knows about it and can imagine it.<br /> <br /> For example to imagine creating a new eye for someone or grow a new arm is something which everyone should possibly be able to do with sufficient dots in the Discipline. But with more advanced stuff like removing, or adding, cancer and so on the Vicissitude-user would probably first need the Medicine dots to know what's going on, sufficient Vicissitude dots to affect this kind of thing and finally Auspex if the material worked is to small to be sensed or observed without Auspex. Such as modifying the cells in some part of the body.<br /> <br /> The reasons for this approach is that I'm mostly interested in historical settings, thus medicine knowledge might not be all that advanced or accessable yet I still want Vicissitude to be able to do stuff, for both NPCs and PCs. But at the same time I don't want Clan Tzimisce to essentially be centuries ahead of humanity in terms of medicine science. It should be more like that the Tzimisce are learning from human progress in scientific fields and getting better with Vicissitude than being, as I said, centuries or millennia ahead of the kine.<br /> <br /> This can lead to alot of grey areas, fuzzy borders and such but I think that it would work better than the &quot;its magic!&quot; or a &quot;correct science is necessary!&quot; approaches would allow when it comes to the actually gaming.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-13T11:55:51-07:00","id":1520539,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1430698-v20-vicissitude-and-physical-impediments?p=1520503#post1520503\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If we treat Vicissitude as similar to mundane surgery, we must modify the question: can a surgeon cure a person's disfigurement?<br /> <br /> The answer, of course, being &quot;Yes&quot; in many cases. That's what plastic surgery is for.<br /> <br /> So it seems pretty clear that Vicissitude should be able to.<br /> <br /> Mechanically, were I the Storyteller in this scenario, I would mandate that getting rid of the Flaw would require buying it off with XP. It's no fair to the other players if one elects to start the PC with Disfigured or Monstrous, then go get in-universe plastic surgery to immediately correct it, maybe with a temporary dip in Resources to cover the cost. If you want to not be ugly anymore, you have to pay off the chargen points you got.<br /> <br /> The surgery - or in this case the Vicissitude - can merely be thought of as the justification for buying off the Flaw. In much the way the PC might get surgery and physical therapy to buy off the Lame Flaw, or go to rehab to shake off an Addiction.<br /> <br /> Obviously, the above mostly applies to mortals. Vampire PCs are more limited in what methods can change their form on a permanent basis. (And, as an aside, Rehab isn't really a possibility for vampires either, for multiple reasons). Vicissitude's utility is not merely that it's flesh-sculpting magic that goes beyond what mundane surgery can do, and more easily/quickly/safely, it's also necessary to permanently change the undead form. Generation permitting, it would just be a matter of choosing not to spend BP healing the &quot;aggravated wounds&quot; that a change represents. (And if you're paying XP alongside it, I as ST would just make it permanent. You wanted it, you got it).</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed on almost everything except the experience usage.<b> Malleable Visage</b> can rise your Appearance, that is the power description, experience on top of that is ignoring the power description and potentially charging the character twice (paying the discipline AND buying the flaw).<br /> <br /> It can be metagamed, yes. A starting Tzimisce could get <b>Monstrous</b>, <b>Short </b>and perhaps <b>Disfigured </b>as starting flaws, and fix it with Vicissitude; but Appearance is the dumb stat and it is the literal power description to fix some of the things. It is similar to say you have a social flaw vs mortals, but you Dominate / Presence them all and the flaw stops being relevant.<br /> <br /> \u200b<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caerolion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1430698-v20-vicissitude-and-physical-impediments?p=1520506#post1520506\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I always go with the idea of Vicissitude requires literal sculpting of the changes. You could increase height, but that mass needs to come from <i>somewhere</i>, so will probably end up thinner/frailer than what they were before. To increase bone length, well, that bone\u2019s gotta come from somewhere else in you, unless you stretch out what\u2019s already there, and weaken it in the process.<br /> Remove cancer <i>cells</i>, that\u2019s a no, but they could certainly remove a tumour.<br /> <br /> Basically, it lets you use your fingers as scalpels/forceps/clay-shaping tools. I\u2019m not really even a fan of it being able to change eye/hair colour, and only accept it because it\u2019s specifically called out as being possible.</div> </div> </div> </div>Totally agreed.\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-15T16:20:15-07:00","id":1520721,"title":"","content":"Vicissitude can do absolutely anything you want. That's why I've banned or severely nerfed it in the games I ST","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27429-microcuchon","name":"Microcuchon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"201"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-08T03:59:53-07:00","id":1536975,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1430698-v20-vicissitude-and-physical-impediments#post1430698\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am curious to the limits of Vicissitude, and I wonder if applied to a mortal, it can:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Heal physical impediments like nearsightedness (myopia)?</li> <li>Heal physical impediments like missing organs?</li> <li>Identify cancerous cells?</li> <li>Remove cancerous cells?</li> <li>Alter cancerous cells so they are no longer cancerous?</li> <li>Remove body fat from the body (liposuction)?</li> </ol><br /> Thanks for the time and attention.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sadly, no. They can only remove freckles from gingers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25666-illuminostro","name":"Illuminostro","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"166"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}